From: fenleon <fenleon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:34:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] voip: land in-tree session work (outbound orientation
 cell, local_video_attached gate, signal_video_stopped, initiator ungate)

Lands the uncommitted 2026-09-25..10-13 session work Task 3 of the
calls resilience plan builds on:

- Outbound device_orientation cell: VideoShared owns an Arc<AtomicU8>,
  shared into the registry entry at registration
  (set_device_orientation/device_orientation), and the signaling
  handler's own <video> sends (upgrade answer / accept announce) read
  it instead of hardcoding 0.
- local_video_attached plane gate: set_video_channels installs a
  teardown hook at registration for every call, so
  begin_local_video_request must gate on the attached ENDPOINTS, not
  video_teardown.is_some(); a pending peer request or a competing
  local request also blocks a begin; stop_local_video releases the
  peer's open request (its own timeout reaps the peer half).
- CallHandle::signal_video_stopped: <video state=6> without tearing the
  plane down, so the peer keeps rendering and a camera-on is just an
  announce + media.
- Video-upgrade initiator ungate experiment (2026-09-25 live session):
  the initiator sends immediately instead of waiting for the peer's
  UpgradeAccept.

Task 3's peer-orientation cell (registry, engine, facade attach) is
NOT in this commit.
